==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|bairro}}, {{m|roa-opt|barrio}}, from {{der|pt|ar|بَرِيّ||savage}}, referring to the outer, surrounding or less civilized or urbanized parts of a city. Compare {{cog|es|barrio}}.

